43:["$","$L47",null,{"children":[["$","$L48",null,{"title":"Every request fails with a permission error","id":"every-request-fails-with-a-permission-error","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Either the workload identity lacks Storage Blob Data Contributor on the\ncontainer, or a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sas_url"}]," has expired. A SAS expiry surfaces as an\nauthentication failure, so check the signature's window before assuming the\nrole assignment is wrong. If the store did not start at all with a message\nabout the Workload Identity credential, the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AZURE_*"}]," variables are missing."]}]}],["$","$L48",null,{"title":"Requests go somewhere unexpected","id":"requests-go-somewhere-unexpected","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"sas_url"}]," wins over everything. If it is set, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"account_name"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"endpoint"}]," play no part in building the URL. Unset it to go back to the derived\nendpoint."]}]}],["$","$L48",null,{"title":"The container is not found","id":"the-container-is-not-found","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The store does not create containers. Create it in the storage account first,\nand check that ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container"}]," matches exactly; container names are lowercase."]}]}],["$","$L48",null,{"title":"Connecting to Azurite fails","id":"connecting-to-azurite-fails","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"endpoint"}]," must include the account path segment:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1"}],", not just the host and port. The\ncontainer is appended to whatever you give. Without ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sas_url"}]," the store still\nneeds the Workload Identity variables to start, and the emulator has to accept\nthe resulting token; a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sas_url"}]," minted for the emulator avoids both."]}]}],["$","$L48",null,{"title":"Blobs exist in the container but Forge reports them missing","id":"blobs-exist-in-the-container-but-forge-reports-them-missing","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"consider_expired_after_s"}],". A non-zero value makes blobs older than that\nwindow invisible on purpose, so they pair with a matching lifecycle rule. If\nyou didn't intend that, set it back to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0"}],"."]}]}]]}]
